# OdySea static-analysis policy. Focus: memory safety and modern C++ hygiene.
# Enforces a subset of the C++ Core Guidelines plus clang's own analyzer.
#
# Two categories are disabled rather than held against the advisory baseline,
# because an advisory diagnostic nobody will ever act on is not a finding, it is
# cover for the next one. The recorded set exists so a genuinely new diagnostic
# is visible in it; several hundred permanent entries make that impossible, and
# a reader who has learned to scroll past the recorded set has learned to scroll
# past a new one too.
#
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access
#       Requires a checked accessor for every subscript. This project subscripts
#       deliberately, after the index has been established by the code that
#       produced it, and in paths where a second bounds check per element is
#       real cost. The class of defect it describes is covered by controls that
#       do not depend on a style rule: clang's own analyzer and the whole
#       bugprone family are errors here rather than advisories, and the entire
#       test suite runs under AddressSanitizer, which reports an out-of-bounds
#       access as a fault at the point it happens rather than as a suggestion.
#
# A category is promoted to an error once the tree is clean of it, so it cannot
# return as one more advisory line. modernize-use-scoped-lock is the first:
# std::scoped_lock is a strict superset of std::lock_guard, so there is no case
# where the older spelling is the right answer, and leaving it advisory would
# have meant re-establishing the same clean state on every future review.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -readability-magic-numbers

WarningsAsErrors: 'bugprone-*,cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,cppcoreguidelines-no-malloc,clang-analyzer-*,modernize-use-scoped-lock'
